# Style Policy: Python Imports

Use module-level imports by default, consistent with PEP 8.

## Rules

- Keep imports at module scope unless doing so causes a concrete problem.
- Use deferred imports only for justified cases such as avoiding an import cycle or isolating a rarely used optional dependency.
- Place a necessary deferred import at the start of the smallest applicable scope and document why it cannot be module-level.
- Use `typing.TYPE_CHECKING` where type-only imports would otherwise create a runtime cycle.
